      "role": "user",
      "content": "so you're saying regulation is basically just a lagging indicator that can't keep up? it sounds like you're arguing that the drive for innovation is so fundamental that it's basically outside of human control. if that's the case, doesn't that mean the social consequences—like mass unemployment or wealth inequality—are just something we have to accept as the price of progress?",
